{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramAddable","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramAddable","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramCorner"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.card_addableCells_eq_card_cornerCells_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.card_addableCells_eq_card_cornerCells_succ","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L288-L294","doc":"**A Young diagram has exactly one more addable cell than it has removable corners.**\n\nThe diagonal of the `DU − UD = I` relation on the Young lattice. Holds for every `μ`,\nincluding the empty diagram (no corners, one addable cell — the box `(0,0)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.card_addableCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.card_addableCells","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L280-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.card_cornerCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.card_cornerCells","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L274-L278","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.mem_addableCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.mem_addableCells","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L255-L272","doc":"`addableCells` is the set of addable cells — the definition by image is faithful. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.mem_cornerCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.mem_cornerCells","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L242-L253","doc":"`cornerCells` is the set of removable corners — the definition by image is faithful. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.addableCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.addableCells","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L237-L240","doc":"The addable cells of `μ`, as a `Finset` of cells. Defined as the image of `addableRows`;\n`mem_addableCells` proves this really is the set of addable cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.cornerCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.cornerCells","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L232-L235","doc":"The removable corners of `μ`, as a `Finset` of cells. Defined as the image of\n`cornerRows`; `mem_cornerCells` proves this really is the set of removable corners. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.card_addableRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.card_addableRows","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L219-L228","doc":"Row count form of the main identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.addableRows_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.addableRows_eq","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L193-L217","doc":"**The shift.** The addable rows are row `0` together with the rows directly below a\nremovable corner. This is the combinatorial heart of the whole file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.addableRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.addableRows","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L189-L191","doc":"The rows that admit an addable cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.cornerRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.cornerRows","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L185-L187","doc":"The rows that end in a removable corner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.addable_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.addable_iff","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L163-L183","doc":"A cell is addable exactly when it sits just past the end of its row, and that row is\neither the first or strictly shorter than the one above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.corner_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.corner_iff","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L153-L161","doc":"A cell is a removable corner exactly when it ends its row and its row is strictly longer\nthan the next. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.card_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.card_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L145-L149","doc":"Adding an addable cell increases the cell count by exactly one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.mem_addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.mem_addCell","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L140-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.addCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.addCell","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L111-L138","doc":"**Cell insertion `μ ∪ {c}`.** Adjoining an addable cell to `μ` yields a Young diagram:\n`insert c μ.cells` is still a lower set, because any `b ≤ c` with `b ≠ c` is `≤` one of `c`'s\nneighbours, which `IsAddableCell` places in `μ`.\n\nThis is what makes `IsAddableCell` a characterisation rather than a bare definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.IsAddableCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.IsAddableCell","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L105-L109","doc":"An **addable cell** of `μ`: a cell outside `μ` whose upper neighbour `(i-1, j)` and left\nneighbour `(i, j-1)` each either lie in `μ` or fall off the board. These are exactly the\ncells that may be adjoined to `μ` with the result still a Young diagram — see `addCell`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.rowLen_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.rowLen_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramAddable.lean#L95-L101","doc":"Row `i` is non-empty exactly when `i` is below the height of the first column. In\nparticular `μ.rowLen i = 0` for every `i ≥ μ.colLen 0`, which is what makes the row-index\nsets below finite. ","signatureChunk":0}]}